  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.84,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.4", "U22.4", "U35.4", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(U15-Y)", "Net-(U15-A)"],
      "observed": "The e-stop buffers are valued SN74LVC1G07, but their metadata specifies the U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R and their symbol has a /OE pin. The 1G125 is a push-pull tri-state buffer, not an open-drain 1G07 sink.",
      "expected": "The specification identifies these e-stop stages as SN74LVC1G07 buffers wired as sinks; the selected parts should therefore provide the intended open-drain sink behavior rather than actively driving the output high.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U36 | SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 | ... MPN=U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "acorn-motherboard:SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 ... pins: 1=/OE(input) ... 4=Y(output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_OUT : ... J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) ... U36.4(Y,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an e-stop loop ... gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is what is fitted, the e-stop output stages can actively drive high instead of releasing the line when not sinking. This can conflict with an external sink-style e-stop loop and undermine the intended fail-safe interface.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The e-stop parts' value, symbol and sourcing metadata disagree: the listed MPN is a push-pull tri-state buffer, whereas the specification describes open-drain sink buffers. If the MPN governs assembly, the e-stop interface may actively drive a line that is intended to be released or sunk."
}

